T DeclaredIntent                    | OutlinerSequence.h | 54-64  | owning                        | -  | One declared intent, complete enough to apply without consulting whoever declared it. ①. Every operand is named here so that what is applied is what was meant. else, and `Declare` admits it with an undeclared subject for exactly that reason.
    has   Declared              OutlinerIntent    [-]  ?
    has   Subject               OccupantIdentity  [-]  ?
    has   RelatedOccupant       OccupantIdentity  [-]  ?
    has   DeclaredName          std::string       [-]  ?
    has   SoughtText            std::string       [-]  ?
    has   OrderWithinEnclosure  std::uint32_t     [-]  ?
    has   StandingEnabled       bool              [-]  ?
    has   SelectionExtended     bool              [-]  ?
    by    Source/OutlinerPanel.cpp, Source/OutlinerSequence.cpp
    note  ⚠️ An intent carrying only "the selection" would apply against whatever the selection had become by
    note  🔴 `Narrow` is the one intent that addresses no occupant. It carries its sought text and nothing

