T OutlinerSequence                  | OutlinerSequence.h | 94-225 | owning                        | -  | Everything `12` owns, reconciled in the one order `12` §4 fixes. · ④ repair enclosure labels · ⑤ rebuild rows and adjust counts · ⑥ re-derive changed subsets · ⑦ re-derive search entries for renamed occupants. Every one of those orderings is load-bearing: ③ before ④ because transforms must be final before anything spatial is derived from them, and ④ before ⑤ because rows rebuilt against stale labels are briefly wrong and are displayed. completed tick left, and `Reconcile` is the only writer of it.
    has   Population           PopulationIndex                [-]  ?
    has   NestingRelations     SceneStructure                 [-]  ?
    has   Linearisation        RowSequence                    [-]  ?
    has   Subsets              EnrollmentIndex                [-]  ?
    has   NameSearch           TrigramIndex                   [-]  ?
    has   Revised              RevisionSequence               [-]  ?
    has   Selected             SelectionSequence              [-]  ?
    has   PendingDeclarations  std::vector<DeclaredIntent>    [-]  ?
    has   RefusedDeclarations  std::vector<RejectedIntent>    [-]  ?
    has   RenamedDeclarations  std::vector<DeclaredIntent>    [-]  ?
    has   WithdrawnOccupants   std::vector<OccupantIdentity>  [-]  ?
    has   LiveGenerations      std::vector<std::uint32_t>     [-]  ?
    has   NarrowingSought      std::string                    [-]  ?
    has   NarrowingOwed        bool                           [-]  ?
    by    Api/OutlinerPanel.h, Source/OutlinerPanel.cpp, Source/OutlinerSequence.cpp
    note  🔴 The tick order is ① apply committed intent · ② reconcile the population · ③ compound attachments
    note  ⚠️ No linearisation is observed between ④ and ⑤ — invariant 10. `Rows()` reads the sequence the last

